    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, my realtor just mentioned something about needing to set up an escrow account for my house purchase here in Toronto. I've never dealt with this before, can you explain what escrow actually is and why it's used during the closing process?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow is a neutral third-party holding account where your deposit and important documents are safely kept until all conditions of the home purchase are met. In Toronto, it protects both you and the seller by ensuring funds aren't released until things like financing, inspections, and title transfer are fully completed. Your realtor will typically use a trust account with a lawyer or brokerage to manage this, so you don't have to worry about handing money directly to the seller.",
